"state":"KS"},{"bioguideId":"C000059","fullName":"Rep. Calvert, Ken [R-CA-41]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"B001298","fullName":"Rep. Bacon, Don [R-NE-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NE"},{"bioguideId":"G000558","fullName":"Rep. Guthrie, Brett [R-KY-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"KY"},{"bioguideId":"F000470","fullName":"Rep. Fischbach, Michelle [R-MN-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MN"},{"bioguideId":"S001228","fullName":"Rep. Schmidt, Derek [R-KS-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"KS"},{"bioguideId":"W000829","fullName":"Rep. Wied, Tony [R-WI-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WI"},{"bioguideId":"E000246","fullName":"Rep. Edwards, Chuck [R-NC-11]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T15:43:45+00:00","id":"hjres10-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-03","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-03","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"10","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Economics and Public Finance","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"N000193","district":3,"fullName":"Rep. Nunn, Zachary [R-IA-3]","party":"R","state":"IA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-03","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p>This joint resolution proposes a constitutional amendment prohibiting total outlays for a fiscal year from exceeding total receipts for that fiscal year unless Congress authorizes the excess by a three-fifths roll call vote of each chamber. The prohibition excludes outlays for repayment of debt principal and receipts derived from borrowing.</p> <p>The amendment requires a three-fifths roll call vote of each chamber to increase the public debt limit. It prohibits a bill to increase revenue from becoming law unless it has been approved by a majority roll call vote of each chamber. </p> <p>The amendment also requires the President to submit an annual budget in which total outlays do not exceed total receipts.</p> <p>Congress may waive these requirements due to a declaration of war or a military conflict that causes an imminent and serious military threat to national security. </p>","updateDate":"2025-01-14T17:26:44Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Proposing a balanced budget amendment to the Constitution of the United States.","type":"hjres","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:07:50Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:07:50Z"}
